{"agent_id":"pp3g-MA65-fix-agents-md-operator-gated-wording-verbal-approval","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-30T19:51:38.329277562Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c5234cf4-e8df-4e3a-a316-9dd440e18ebf","comment_uuid":"9cce4155-d67a-4203-a075-0de5e3187ca2","author":"pp3g-MA65-fix-agents-md-operator-gated-wording-verbal-approval","content":"Plan: Fix the Model Discipline — Operator-Gated wording per operator directive 2026-08-30 (verbal approval required and sufficient; no Crosslink approval comment; per-launch scoping).\n\nSCOPE:\n1. AGENTS.md (assigned target): replace the 'Required 4 steps before retry' bullet with the 3-step process — 1) question (verbal approval via question tool, required and sufficient), 2) opencode models verify exact ID, 3) retry. Add: no Crosslink approval comment (do not post or wait for one — operator never runs shell commands per D1–D4; a durable approval comment would be misread by future agents as standing acceptance and breaks per-launch scoping). Add: approval is per-launch unless the operator explicitly says it covers multiple phases. Keep all other bullets (mechanically-enforced gate description, cheaper-first, free-tier guidance, prefix note, model-discipline.md pointer) unchanged.\n\n2. PROPAGATION (same conceptual change, documented decision): the identical 4-step approval-comment wording exists in .crosslink/knowledge/model-discipline.md (§7, lines 36–42) and docs/ORCHESTRATOR.md (Model Selection section, lines 589–595). AGENTS.md designates model-discipline.md as the mandatory model-list doc; leaving both mirrors mandating the Crosslink comment would preserve the pathological process the operator directive removes. Per AGENTS.md Repository Changes rule (update documentation where conceptual changes occur), I will apply the same wording fix to both mirrors in a separate commit so it is independently reviewable/revertable.\n\nDISCOVERY (reported, NOT fixed — out of scope): the mechanical gate still enforces the old process. crosslink-guard.ts (hasApprovalForModel, lines 843–869, invoked at 1479) and orchestrator-guard.ts (line 284) hard-block gated launches unless issues.db has an --kind approval comment containing the exact --model ID. After this doc fix, a compliant 3-step verbal-approval launch will still be blocked at retry, and the block message itself instructs posting the approval comment. Recommend a companion issue to align the gate code (e.g. keep active-issue check + block signature; drop the DB approval-comment check, since verbal approval cannot be mechanically verified). I will not modify guard code in this issue.\n\nVerification: grep confirms no remaining 'approval comment' / '--kind approval' mandates in the three docs; markdown structure intact; commit per doc group.","created_at":"2026-08-30T19:51:38.322652833Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:114LrjMPMzb0zvrkAq9XyLWG1N5h5mVLOoirb2seIyo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2N1Tgd+G7xdRtLFLxRe0EzRNYzc/XizWHuO/dF6SYyQAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAJgx4nJsWjBKRAp7IPVQM1eC0pcKeSR6XOSDexfaoWPLUA24Y9Lieu27cBTsvCovMdjmSWin8MlsBvbsJ9dbIAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:114LrjMPMzb0zvrkAq9XyLWG1N5h5mVLOoirb2seIyo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2N1Tgd+G7xdRtLFLxRe0EzRNYzc/XizWHuO/dF6SYyQAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKkcK1G3HYS1LURwTi0ZZVeMOgGJZLaXOHHD4VxKruN4TmhAExeYFWlrYQcZ0mqKdsI7ib/Pfxk7tH20UOHXcQU="}
